capability stream/standard  the process's own input, output and error output
  heroes  io.stdin, io.stdout, io.stderr
  go      -
  rust    stdin, stdout, stderr, Stdin, Stdout, Stderr
  python  -
  note    Go's are `os.Stdin` and the rest, and Python's `sys.stdin` and the rest, outside this area. Here they are borrowed: `close` empties the place and closes nothing, as Rust's cannot be closed

capability stream/pipe  a pipe's two ends
  heroes  io.pipe
  go      io.Pipe, io.PipeReader, io.PipeWriter, io.PipeReader.Read, io.PipeWriter.Write
  rust    pipe, PipeReader, PipeWriter
  python  -
  note    Rust's: a pipe of the system, its writes buffered by the system. Go's is a pipe in memory where each write waits for its read; a pipe here waits only once the system's buffer is full

capability stream/close  a stream ended, saying whether its last bytes could be written
  heroes  io.close
  go      io.Closer, io.PipeReader.Close, io.PipeWriter.Close
  rust    -
  python  IOBase.close
  note    Rust closes on drop and says nothing. A second close fails `closed`, as Go's second `Close` of a file fails, where Python's answers nothing: a closed stream is closed to every later call

capability stream/close-with-error  a pipe's end closed so its other end reads a given error
  heroes  refused: a pipe of the system carries bytes and an end, never an error value
  go      io.PipeReader.CloseWithError, io.PipeWriter.CloseWithError
  rust    -
  python  -

