  python  RawIOBase.read, FileIO.read, RawIOBase.readinto, BufferedIOBase.read1, BufferedIOBase.readinto, BufferedIOBase.readinto1
  note    it answers a new list where the three fill the caller's; at most 65,536 bytes at once, so a count from outside never sizes a buffer. The end is an empty list, as Go's 0 with EOF and Rust's Ok(0)

