capability failure/codes  what a failed call of a stream says
  heroes  io.last_failure
  go      io.EOF, io.ErrClosedPipe
  rust    Error, ErrorKind, Error::kind, Error::raw_os_error, Error::last_os_error, Error::from_raw_os_error, Error::new, Error::other, Error::get_ref, Error::get_mut, Error::into_inner, Error::downcast, RawOsError, Result, const_error
  python  BlockingIOError, UnsupportedOperation
  note    a failure is a code of README § A4 and a message holding the system's number; the end is no failure here, as Go's EOF is one. The floor's kinds map one way each: closed for a stream closed or a reader gone, `timeout` and `stopped` for a socket's stream

